From: GibaxLeGrand <48137851+GibaxLeGrand@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 14:00:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 19/24] Runner: the players' tags over their racers (SRNP_TAGS)

SRNP_TAGS=TAG0,TAG1,... (seat k = racer k, up to 8 characters, upper
case) puts each player's tag over the "nP" label of the racer they drive;
none for a CPU, none over the player's own racer (the game's or the
spotter's choice, as for the label).

The tags come from a second texture of ours in the srnp_etiquettes block
(version 4: 128x128 C4, one 16-texel row per seat, zero in the file), which
the runner writes with its own pixel font: 7 texels high, 2-texel uprights
and 1-texel bars like the game's labels, white to grey with a navy outline
(the game's text font, "EnglishNormal_game", only has the letters its
English texts use). The routine (now 72 words) draws a second quad over
the label, centred, from that texture with a UV table of ours, in white.
Its entry and table sit after the routine in the same code padding
(0x80004F00-0x80005000). The block stays within the size the game loads
from a save state (GTSE 0xAD7A0 decompressed, 246548 bytes compressed).

Measured (2 runners, 8 seats in lockstep, one with labels and tags, one
without): 29 checksums equal, 0 divergences in JIT64; 24 equal, 0
divergences native.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
